Privacy Policy — Heirloom: Merge & Restore

Last updated: 11 November 2026

[Omer Faruk Celik], [Başakşehir / İstanbul] ("we", "us") makes the game Heirloom: Merge & Restore ("the game"). This policy explains what data the game uses, why, and your choices. Contact: omerfarukcelik58@gmail.com

1. Summary
- You can play the whole game without accepting analytics or personalised ads.
- We do not ask for your name, e-mail address or phone number. There are no accounts. Your game progress is stored only on your device.
- You can change your consent at any time in Settings → Privacy options. Uninstalling the game deletes the data on your device.

2. What we use, why, and on what legal basis
- App-instance ID, gameplay events (for example "task completed", "room finished") and coarse device info (model, OS, language, country).
  Purpose: understand and improve the game, balance the economy.
  Legal basis: your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a); KVKK Art. 5(1)).
  Kept for: 14 months.
- Crash reports (stack trace, device model, OS version, app version).
  Purpose: fix crashes and keep the game stable.
  Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working app (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f); KVKK Art. 5(2)(f)).
  Kept for: 90 days.
- Advertising ID (Android advertising ID / iOS IDFA) and ad interactions.
  Purpose: show optional rewarded videos; personalise them only if you agree.
  Legal basis: your consent (collected through Google's consent tool; on iOS also Apple's App Tracking Transparency).
  Kept for: according to Google's policies (see section 4).
- Remote configuration requests (Firebase installation ID).
  Purpose: adjust game balance (prices, timings, event dates) without an app update.
  Legal basis: legitimate interest in a balanced game (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f); KVKK Art. 5(2)(f)).
  Kept for: according to Google's Firebase terms.
- Your consent choices.
  Purpose: prove and respect your choice.
  Legal basis: legal obligation.
  Kept for: as long as the choice is valid.

Your progress and backups: the save file stays on your phone; we do not receive it. If your phone's own backup is on (Google backup on Android, iCloud on iOS), Google or Apple may include it in that backup under your account and restore it on a new phone.

We do not sell your personal data and do not use it for automated decisions with legal effects.

3. Ads
Ads appear only when you choose to watch a rewarded video (for example to refill energy). If you decline personalised ads, Google may still show non-personalised ads, which use limited data such as approximate location (from your IP address) and the current app. On iOS we ask for tracking permission only after your first play session, only if personalised ads are enabled and you agreed in our consent screen.

4. Service providers and international transfers
- Google LLC / Google Ireland Limited: Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, Firebase Remote Config, Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) and the User Messaging Platform (consent). See https://policies.google.com/privacy and https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
- Apple Inc. and Google LLC: app stores.

Some providers process data outside your country, including in the United States. For transfers from the EU/UK we rely on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is certified, or on Standard Contractual Clauses. For transfers from Türkiye we rely on the safeguards set out in Article 9 of the Turkish Personal Data Protection Law (KVKK).

5. Deleting your data
- Uninstalling the game deletes all game data stored on your device.
- To withdraw consent for analytics and ads, open Settings → Privacy options in the game.
- To ask us to delete data held by our providers, e-mail [CONTACT EMAIL] with the subject "Data deletion – Heirloom". Because we hold only pseudonymous data (no name or e-mail), we may ask for the app-instance ID shown in Settings to find your data. We answer within 30 days. Analytics data is deleted automatically after 14 months and crash reports after 90 days.

6. Your rights
Depending on where you live, you may ask to access, correct, delete or export your data, to restrict or object to processing, and to withdraw consent at any time (this does not affect processing before the withdrawal). Contact us at [CONTACT EMAIL]. You may also complain to your data protection authority (in Türkiye: Kişisel Verileri Koruma Kurumu; in the EU/UK: your local supervisory authority).

7. Children
The game is made for adults and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 13 (or the higher age required in your country). If you believe a child has given us data, contact us and we will delete it.

8. Security
Data is sent encrypted (HTTPS) and stored with our providers' security measures. No method is 100% secure.

9. Changes
If this policy changes, we will update the date above and, for important changes, tell you in the game.

10. Contact
